# Testing Guidelines

## Backend Testing (Jest + Supertest)

### Test Structure
```javascript
describe('Auth Controller', () => {
  describe('POST /api/auth/register', () => {
    it('should register a new user with valid credentials', async () => {
      // Arrange
      const userData = { email: 'test@test.com', password: 'password123', username: 'testuser' };
      
      // Act
      const response = await request(app).post('/api/auth/register').send(userData);
      
      // Assert
      expect(response.status).toBe(201);
      expect(response.body.success).toBe(true);
      expect(response.body.data.user.email).toBe(userData.email);
    });
    
    it('should not register user with existing email', async () => {
      // Test implementation
    });
  });
});
```

### Unit Tests (`/backend/tests/unit`)
Test individual functions in isolation:
- Password hashing functions
- JWT token generation/verification
- Data validation functions
- Utility functions
- Model methods

### Integration Tests (`/backend/tests/integration`)
Test API endpoints with database:
- Use mongodb-memory-server for in-memory database
- Test complete request-response cycle
- Test authentication flow
- Test CRUD operations
- Test error handling

### Test Coverage Goals
- Aim for 70%+ overall coverage
- 100% coverage for critical functions (auth, payment)
- Run `npm test -- --coverage` to check coverage

## Frontend Testing (Flutter)

### Unit Tests (`/frontend/test/unit`)
```dart
void main() {
  group('User Model', () {
    test('fromJson should parse JSON correctly', () {
      final json = {'_id': '1', 'email': 'test@test.com', 'username': 'test'};
      final user = User.fromJson(json);
      
      expect(user.id, '1');
      expect(user.email, 'test@test.com');
      expect(user.username, 'test');
    });
  });
}
```

### Widget Tests (`/frontend/test/widget`)
```dart
void main() {
  testWidgets('Login screen has email and password fields', (WidgetTester tester) async {
    await tester.pumpWidget(MaterialApp(home: LoginScreen()));
    
    expect(find.byType(TextField), findsNWidgets(2));
    expect(find.text('Email'), findsOneWidget);
    expect(find.text('Password'), findsOneWidget);
  });
}
```

### Integration Tests (`/frontend/test/integration`)
Test complete user flows:
- Login flow: enter credentials → submit → navigate to home
- Registration flow
- Profile update flow

## Manual Testing Checklist

### Authentication
- [ ] User can register with valid credentials
- [ ] Cannot register with existing email
- [ ] Cannot register with invalid email format
- [ ] Cannot register with short password
- [ ] User can login with correct credentials
- [ ] Cannot login with wrong password
- [ ] Cannot login with non-existent email
- [ ] Token is stored after login
- [ ] Token persists after page refresh
- [ ] User is auto-logged in if token exists
- [ ] User can logout successfully
- [ ] Token is removed after logout

### Profile
- [ ] User can view their profile
- [ ] User can edit profile fields
- [ ] Changes are saved to backend
- [ ] Points and achievements display correctly
- [ ] Avatar upload works (if implemented)

### Protected Routes
- [ ] Unauthenticated users cannot access protected routes
- [ ] Authenticated users can access protected routes
- [ ] Expired tokens are handled properly

### Error Handling
- [ ] Network errors show user-friendly messages
- [ ] Validation errors are displayed clearly
- [ ] Server errors are handled gracefully
- [ ] Loading states work correctly

## Testing Best Practices

### Backend
- Mock external dependencies
- Use before/after hooks for setup/teardown
- Test both success and failure cases
- Test edge cases and boundary conditions
- Keep tests independent (no shared state)
- Use descriptive test names

### Frontend
- Mock API calls in unit/widget tests
- Test user interactions (button clicks, form inputs)
- Test navigation between screens
- Test state changes
- Test error states and loading states
- Use descriptive test names

### General
- Write tests before or alongside code (TDD/BDD)
- Run tests before committing code
- Fix failing tests immediately
- Keep tests simple and readable
- Don't test implementation details, test behavior
- Maintain test code quality like production code
